WEBVTT

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:11.230
With the rapid development of Hyper Technology came the Labor...

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:15.330
a multi-purpose, humanoid construction machine whose use...

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.240
spread into almost every field.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:23.280
However, this gave rise to a new threat to society: Labor crime.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:31.260
The Tokyo Metro Police founded the Special Vehicles, Section 2...

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.620
within the Security Division to combat these ever-growing crimes.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:41.670
This was the beginning of the SV2 Patrol Labor... Patlabor... units.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:03.080
kimi ni ikarete METAMETA MECHAMEKA gurui
You really threw a wrench into my works

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:09.560
HAATO BIITO wo awaserya sore de ikisou yo
If I can get my heartbeat under control, I think I'll make it

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:15.270
kimi to atashi wa miraiha koi no TEKUNISHAN
We're futurists, you and me; technicians of love

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:20.910
takaku hayaku suki yo ki mama ni
Higher, faster, I'll love you if I want to

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:27.460
METARU BODII no hadazawari sae
I think I'll get to like

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:33.400
atsuku kanjite kuru kuse ni narisou
The way I get flushed at the touch of your metal body

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:39.690
CHACHI na Imagination koeta jigen de
Oh, don't stop this gravity-defying feeling

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:46.580
juuryokuihan ah nukeru Feeling tomenai de
That goes way beyond mere imagination

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:53.100
kimi ni ikarete METAMETA MECHAMEKA gurui
You really threw a wrench into my works

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:59.550
PITAri kakarerya PIKAA kireru ARUFONSU
When I hold him tight, my Alphonse can do anything

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:05.180
kimi to atashi wa miraiha koi no TEKUNISHAN
We're futurists, you and me; technicians of love

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:13.760
sora mo umi mo kyou mo ashita mo Nothin' impossible
Anytime, anywhere, nothing's impossible

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:17.720
Nothing's impossible

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.130
Second Unit... vacation

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:55.220
Huh? Weren't you supposed to go on vacation today?

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:59.350
I am. Well, I'm on vacation, but I thought... you know...

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:03.690
With us on vacation, it must be tough on you guys...

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:08.130
so maybe I could help out and make myself useful or something.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:14.170
I appreciate the sentiment, but that's not necessary.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.830
If something comes up, you'll be called in anyway...

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.380
so why don't you go to your apartment and get some sleep?

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:23.310
Your gang of delinquents is living it up back home.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.820
It must be nice to have someplace to go home <i>to</i>.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:31.890
All right, then. How about putting on some coffee for starters?

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:53.290
Shinohara Heavy Industries      Hachiouji

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:04.550
Don't! You can't!

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:06.130
Don't worry about it!

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:09.020
I <i>said</i>, you shouldn't be in here!

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:10.620
Get lost!

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:12.930
Okay, this way.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.230
That area's off-limits!

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:15.860
You can't come in here!

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:19.410
Asuma!

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:21.240
Hey, Jeets. How's it going?

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.770
For Heaven's sake...

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:34.150
the few times you <i>do</i> come here, it's always out of the blue.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:39.960
No! Don't!

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.490
You <i>can't</i>!

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:46.670
If the president found out... If it were leaked to <i>outsiders</i>...

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.000
Please, your old friend Jitsuyama is begging you!

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.590
Stop!

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:53.000
I saw it all.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.880
So what're you gonna use a behemoth like <i>this</i> for?

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:58.500
That's restricted information!

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.140
Nothing's restricted from the president's son.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:03.150
C'mon, you can tell me!

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:05.520
Your father doesn't trust you at all.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.850
Its drive system is two SCLMs...

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:12.090
upgraded from the kind we use in the SV2.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:17.330
This is good, but this independent custom computer...

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:20.130
and 64-gigabyte CD-ROM in the shoulder here...

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:24.100
Why would a Labor need an FCS?

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:25.670
Hey, wait a minute.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:27.710
Don't tell me this is for <i>military</i> use!

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:31.140
It is, but it's still in the testing stage, though.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:34.770
Your father wants to take on Yotsubishi with it.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:38.010
With construction on the first phase of the Babylon Project finished...

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:40.420
and sales to private firms leveling off...

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:45.050
I can understand why we'd have to worm our way into military market.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:47.390
There's a world of difference between this...

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:51.330
and those overblown armored car Type-97s that they're using now.

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:54.630
If this works, you've really put the know-how you got from...

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:57.300
developing the Patlabors to use in a strange way.

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:59.940
By the way, have you gone to see your father yet?

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.010
We started fighting the instant we saw each other.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:04.370
And it would've been worse if I'd known about <i>this</i>.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:05.570
That's too bad.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:08.050
You haven't gone home in such a long time.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:09.240
Who cares?

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:11.310
So I can't go home, big deal.

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:13.750
There's plenty of other places I can go.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:17.560
Um, Tamiko?

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:21.820
You <i>know</i> it's dangerous to use cutlery when you're worked up.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:26.000
He's not <i>staying</i> here, is he? We don't have a spare bed!

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.630
What if he hears? That's embarrassing!

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:34.100
But you promised that we'd spend your vacation together!

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:37.770
Just the two of us! You said you'd pamper me!

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:39.010
I haven't forgotten!

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:41.170
We can do the shopping together, okay?

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:42.550
Um...

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:45.920
I just remembered someplace that I need to go.

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:47.720
I'll be going now.

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:50.360
Oh, are you sure? Well, take your time!

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:54.490
Dinner will be ready soon, but we only have two strips of meat.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:56.620
Miki? Why don't you set out some beer?

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:59.460
Oh, right. I'm sorry I was so inconsiderate.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:06.500
You may think I'm pathetic now, but you'll understand someday!

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:13.870
Talk about forward, you didn't even call.

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:16.750
What if I hadn't been here?

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:18.340
But you <i>are</i>.

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.350
- Come on in.
- This is a hold up!

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:33.260
Thanks, but jokes like that are bad for your health.

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:38.970
The JSDF has left to participate in LIMPAC 99, the US-Japan...

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:43.030
circum-pan-Pacific Joint Maneuvers, which began today.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:48.100
And in response to the burgeoning defense budget, there is a call...

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:51.520
for discussion, in conjunction with opposition party movements...

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:53.610
to cut it back once again to 1%.

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:58.850
As always, many ships and aircraft are participating this year.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:00.450
They include:

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:02.120
15 transport escorts...

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:04.100
12 submarines...

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.860
- 5 tankers...
- Hey.

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:07.700
18 frigates...

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:09.700
25 sub-spotting planes.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:11.670
Aren't you going anywhere?

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:16.070
You're gonna spend your whole vacation here in front of the TV?

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:20.210
Don't be ridiculous. I'm going back.

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:21.420
Back?

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.920
I couldn't get a ticket...

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:25.490
so I'm taking the morning flight the day after tomorrow.

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:29.720
It won't be much more than a day trip, but I want to see my grandma.

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:32.890
Your grandmother, huh?

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:37.300
Yeah. That's something to go home for.

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:39.060
And in other news...

00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:41.900
A woman claiming to be the common-law wife of...

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.800
designer Yutaka Buchiyama, age 33, whose nude body was...

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:46.460
found in his home office last April...

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:58.820
If I go back to the dorms now and get drunk alone...

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:01.550
I may as well just hang it up.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:22.410
Izumi Liquors

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:36.760
Being a cop keeps you so busy that you can only come home at New Year's?

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:42.990
You know Naoko down the street? She's getting married this summer.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.430
You should, too!

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:49.000
You can't spend your whole life driving those robots around!

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.730
He's a <i>Labor</i>, not a robot.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:56.170
Whatever! A woman shouldn't be doing such dangerous work!

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:59.210
It'll be a catastrophe if you get hurt and can't get married!

00:09:59.310 --> 00:10:01.610
If you get hurt, it'll be too late!

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:03.680
I'm done.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:08.650
Who does she get this from?

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.830
But I like <i>Alphonse</i>.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.960
Really? Is that the only reason?

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:27.410
Oh, I don't know.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.510
Noa! Telephone!

00:10:29.610 --> 00:10:32.010
It's from some boy named Shinohara.

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:34.180
Shinohara?

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:37.540
Coming! I'll be right there!

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.310
Geez! How long were you gonna keep me waiting?

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:44.690
Hey, I thought you might be bored...

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:47.590
so I figured we might go out and do something.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:49.390
Huh?

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:52.060
I <i>said</i>, do you wanna go and do something?

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:54.970
Really? You mean it?

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:57.560
I'll call again when I get there, so come and pick me up, okay?

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:00.570
By the way, where did you say you live?

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:03.340
Huh? Tomakomai?

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:06.680
Wait, the Tomakomai in <i>Hokkaido</i>?

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:10.850
Why the hell do you live so far away?

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:18.940
Clearance 2.8 Meters

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:30.830
I'm sorry, but I'll need to see your license.

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:32.130
Is something wrong?

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:34.300
No, it's just a general check.

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:46.010
- Everything's in order.
- Thanks.

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:48.290
Hold on!

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:52.590
That's a Labor you have in back, right? Do you have a permit?

00:11:53.330 --> 00:11:55.460
You <i>do</i> know that you need a permit to transport...

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.190
general-purpose Labors, don't you?

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:58.700
Um, sure.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:00.500
Could you step out of the truck, please?

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:06.040
I must've forgotten it.

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:17.570
This is the Trans-Tohoku Highway checkpoint at Ichinoseki!

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:20.420
A large trailer carrying a suspicious Labor has just...

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:23.010
broken through the checkpoint and fled the scene!

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:28.660
We're being followed.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:30.160
We have no choice, then.

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:34.800
Master Sergeant, you're cleared to fire. Take them out.

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:07.760
Ground Self-Defense Forces

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:12.770
<i>Patlabor</i>

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:17.770
<i>Patlabor</i>

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.770
Tomakomai Station
\h
