\h


00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:29.780
Fresh Noodles

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:35.070
And in other news, a trailer broke through a police checkpoint...

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:38.160
fled, and opened fire on pursuing patrol cars.

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:43.380
At 11:20 last night near Ichinoseki on the Trans-Tohoku Highway...

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:46.970
a large trailer with Kanagawa plates suddenly broke through...

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:50.740
a general mobile traffic police crackdown checkpoint.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.510
Patrol cars pursued the trailer...

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:54.550
Mister! Gimme a croquette chaser.

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:55.780
Sure.

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:58.290
but they were suddenly fired upon.

00:13:58.390 --> 00:14:01.120
Witnesses have described a brief burst of gunfire...

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:03.790
- C'mon in.
- Egg.

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:06.300
which may have been a large-caliber machine gun.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.300
Could I get a bowl of steaming hot noodles?

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:10.060
Sure, coming right up.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:17.810
- Gimme some bean curd.
- Punk.

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:21.210
Sorry, could I get that without scallions?

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:24.410
Uh... Sure. Here you go.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:47.430
Thanks. This is the only way to go when you're cold.

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:50.240
You from Tokyo?

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:07.160
Asuma!

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:10.290
- Sorry!
- You sure took your time!

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:12.300
- How much do I owe you?
- Forget it.

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:13.990
Really? Talk about lucky!

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:16.100
Let's go!

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:20.290
Come <i>on</i>!

00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:24.970
These guys just don't look like your usual out-of-town Labor nuts.

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:26.040
Public Security, maybe?

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:29.580
No, they have that expression that says "uniform"...

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:32.810
but I don't see why cops would stake out other cops.

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:37.280
How long have they been there?

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:40.360
I first noticed them two or three days ago.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:43.620
I figured that maybe one of those environmental protection groups...

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:46.360
picked us as the target of their next attack.

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:49.630
So that's why you stayed here.

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:51.330
Among other things.

00:15:51.940 --> 00:15:53.500
Sitting here won't help anything.

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:56.130
Our best bet is to go out and ask them directly.

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:57.370
Hey! Wait!

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:13.250
You can't be serious!

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:16.950
The kids have been working night and day to finish overhauling...

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:20.500
all three Labors before your unit gets back from vacation!

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:24.160
But to send just <i>one</i> of them to the manufacturer for maintenance?

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:26.240
Why? What do you think is going to happen?

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:29.430
We can get the job done in time without you doing that!

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:32.410
Try to have a little more faith in us, okay?

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:33.980
Look, I'm sorry.

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:37.380
Would you mind telling me why, Goto?

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:41.080
Just call it a hunch, I guess.

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:46.160
Shige, load Unit 1 onto its trailer.

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:48.650
Chief?

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:51.520
I don't mind you shipping it to the manufacturer...

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:55.430
- but I can't take it there for you.
- That's taken care of.

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:06.470
We finally get a vacation...

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:10.040
so how come I have to go out on a drive with <i>you</i>, Captain?

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:14.420
Besides, driving these things is Yamazaki's or Shinshi's job!

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:17.750
Yamazaki's in Okinawa, and Shinshi's married.

00:17:17.860 --> 00:17:21.550
Besides, don't you always say that justice never goes on vacation?

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:24.460
Then tell me who we're fighting.

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:28.290
They haven't shown themselves yet. The light's changed.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:31.170
There sure isn't much traffic today.

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:33.430
That's because it looks like it's going to snow.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:36.240
Nobody wants to go outside on a day like this.

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:47.650
Wow!

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.650
Okay, pops! Chug it!

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:56.090
You liquor store owners can sure hold your booze, all right!

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:57.420
Huh?

00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:00.090
Noa! Go and grab another bottle from the store.

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:02.100
You're gonna drink some <i>more</i>?

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:05.730
What, so now you're not gonna do what I tell you?

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:07.140
What's with <i>you</i>?

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:10.070
The pilot shall act in accordance with Command's orders!

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:12.800
You'll have to write out another apology for breaking regulations.

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:15.440
There you go again, spouting off.

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:18.380
You always make <i>me</i> do the dirty work.

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:21.780
Hey, don't I always tell you that partners are two in one?

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:23.290
All right, all right.

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:25.550
Officer Izumi, now departing!

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:27.020
That's better!

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:30.630
Forget it. I'm going to bed.

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:35.390
Was it something I said?

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:38.560
No, maybe he's jealous.

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:40.610
Huh? What're you talking about?

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:45.640
Hey, what do you think the Captain's up to?

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:47.800
Probably enjoying his time off...

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:50.780
trying to talk Captain Nagumo into a date. And...

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:52.080
What else? He gets shot down!

00:18:52.180 --> 00:18:53.310
Bingo!

00:18:58.960 --> 00:19:00.930
Hello, Nagumo residence.

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:03.320
Oh? Mr. Goto?

00:19:03.430 --> 00:19:05.990
Thank you for looking after my Shinobu.

00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:07.460
One moment, please.

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:13.170
Hello?

00:19:28.550 --> 00:19:31.720
So what's the big idea, calling me all the way out here?

00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:34.490
There's something I need to talk to you about tonight.

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:38.260
I don't think it <i>is</i>, but there's no telling if my phone is bugged.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:41.860
Actually, there's something I need to tell <i>you</i>.

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:44.040
Okay, you go first.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:48.770
The Labor carried by that trailer that broke through that checkpoint...

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:50.900
may have been a military one.

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.210
I got a call after you left for Hachiouji:

00:19:54.780 --> 00:19:57.680
Based on the bullet holes in the squad cars and the casings...

00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:59.940
recovered from the highway, the gun they used was...

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:03.490
A 20mm Line Metal MK22.

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:08.080
It was developed as a mini-gun for use in NATO gunships.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:11.560
It's also mounted on the G-SDF's Type-97 Labors.

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:16.430
Your sources come through in a hurry, all right.

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:19.890
They say that HQ is in a panic.

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:22.410
With LIMPAC still going on, it looks like it'll take...

00:20:22.510 --> 00:20:25.480
a couple of days just to do a check of all their equipment.

00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:28.550
This is no guided rocket launcher or sub-machine gun.

00:20:28.650 --> 00:20:30.980
This is something that needs a <i>lot</i> of maintenance.

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:34.950
Even if they stole one, terrorists just couldn't handle it.

00:20:35.090 --> 00:20:36.050
What are you getting at?

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:39.820
I'm saying it was used by the people it was <i>issued</i> to in the first place.

00:20:39.930 --> 00:20:43.330
And even if we connect it to them, what if something's looming...

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:46.260
on the horizon that will make it all a moot point?

00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:53.730
You can't possibly think that...

00:20:53.840 --> 00:20:56.900
I do. But I'm just going on circumstantial evidence.

00:20:57.010 --> 00:21:01.110
I might become a laughing stock, but I don't want to regret anything.

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:03.270
That's why I came to talk to you.

00:21:04.250 --> 00:21:06.340
You'll give me a hand, right?

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:19.860
I'm sorry. You may wind up taking the fall for this.

00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:22.990
I never could count on the Second Unit in the first place.

00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:31.010
Shinobu?

00:23:13.210 --> 00:23:15.080
Search the place and dig everybody out!

00:23:15.180 --> 00:23:16.880
Shoot anybody who resists!

00:23:17.150 --> 00:23:21.850
Hey! Where the hell do you think you are, dirtbags?

00:23:26.390 --> 00:23:28.120
You're in charge here?

00:23:28.230 --> 00:23:31.290
We're commandeering all the Labors here!

00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:34.920
So would you mind handing over their startup disks?

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:39.100
Captain! The other hangar's empty! Nobody's here!

00:23:39.310 --> 00:23:40.530
What?

00:23:40.740 --> 00:23:42.040
What's going on here?

00:23:42.140 --> 00:23:43.300
That's impossible!

00:23:43.410 --> 00:23:46.380
I had lookouts on every road to and from this place!

00:23:46.480 --> 00:23:49.540
There hasn't been a single car out of here since yesterday!

00:23:49.650 --> 00:23:50.880
The <i>bay</i>?

00:23:50.980 --> 00:23:54.280
You loaded them onto your boat and shipped them out at night!

00:23:54.390 --> 00:23:55.680
<i>Didn't</i> you?

00:23:57.520 --> 00:24:00.750
Captain! Message from the platoon that left for police headquarters!

00:24:00.860 --> 00:24:04.560
Three Type-98 Labors have appeared at HQ's front gate!

00:24:04.800 --> 00:24:06.130
What?

00:24:06.230 --> 00:24:07.760
Attention, commanders!

00:24:07.870 --> 00:24:10.030
If you wish to avoid meaningless combat...

00:24:10.140 --> 00:24:13.430
lift your siege and leave the area immediately!

00:24:13.910 --> 00:24:19.280
As a point of honor, if we must fight, we will do so to our utmost!

00:24:19.380 --> 00:24:22.780
If blood is spilled here, Japan's 30,000 police officers...

00:24:22.880 --> 00:24:26.720
will see you as the enemy and fight you to the last man!

00:24:27.050 --> 00:24:31.250
I repeat, lift your siege and leave the area immediately!

00:24:32.860 --> 00:24:34.330
Message from the Decisive Action Unit.

00:24:34.430 --> 00:24:37.950
All objectives within the city have been occupied and neutralized.

00:24:38.060 --> 00:24:39.830
- But...
- But? But <i>what</i>?

00:24:39.930 --> 00:24:43.270
Our forces are still in a standoff with a Metro Police Labor unit...

00:24:43.370 --> 00:24:45.960
that was apparently lying in wait for them at Sakuradamon.

00:24:52.180 --> 00:24:53.910
Goto.

00:25:04.860 --> 00:25:07.160
You really did it this time, Kai.

00:25:07.260 --> 00:25:11.130
Just you wait, I'll hunt you down. Count on it.

00:25:16.670 --> 00:25:20.260
Shinobu? If things get hairy, get out of there.

00:25:21.210 --> 00:25:23.670
Not that she'd listen.

00:25:31.220 --> 00:25:34.650
Grandma? I won't be able to make it. Sorry.

00:25:35.190 --> 00:25:38.450
We have learned that the Decisive Action Unit consists of...

00:25:38.560 --> 00:25:42.390
You! It's you! <i>You're</i> who we're up against!

00:25:42.760 --> 00:25:45.750
Don't go! I don't want you to go!

00:25:46.170 --> 00:25:48.400
Tamiko! Don't! Let go!

00:26:07.950 --> 00:26:10.250
Did you pay your respects to your father?

00:26:11.420 --> 00:26:14.290
I won't be able to come home again until summer.

00:26:14.890 --> 00:26:16.290
Take care.

00:26:16.500 --> 00:26:18.220
Don't worry about me.

00:26:19.430 --> 00:26:21.060
I'll write.

00:26:29.840 --> 00:26:30.810
Mom...

00:26:30.910 --> 00:26:34.470
Get going, Hiromi! You'll miss your bus.

00:26:46.590 --> 00:26:49.820
Many buildings are currently occupied, including the Diet...

00:26:49.930 --> 00:26:53.490
the Kabuto Stock Exchange, the NHK Broadcast Center...

00:26:53.600 --> 00:26:55.090
This is bad.

00:26:55.200 --> 00:26:56.170
Let's go, Asuma!

00:26:56.270 --> 00:26:59.700
If we don't do something, Labor units will lose their reputation!

00:27:01.890 --> 00:27:08.890
The uprising's mastermind: Kiyoteru Kai

00:27:15.420 --> 00:27:17.890
Let's go to Tokyo, Noa.

00:27:32.400 --> 00:27:37.270
A war was waiting for us in Tokyo.

00:27:43.260 --> 00:27:47.720
The SV2's Longest Day
Part 1

00:28:47.510 --> 00:28:49.610
Consider everybody outside our unit as hostile?

00:28:49.720 --> 00:28:52.050
Forced to stand alone because of pressure from above...

00:28:52.150 --> 00:28:53.480
does the Second Unit stand a chance?

00:28:53.590 --> 00:28:55.710
And what's the trump card that Kai's holding?

00:28:55.820 --> 00:28:58.950
Orders have come down for your arrest, Captain Goto.

00:28:59.090 --> 00:29:02.060
Next time! The SV2's Longest Day: Part 2!

00:29:02.350 --> 00:29:04.060
Target, lock on!
